@c -*-texinfo-*-
@node gpui-miniapp Manual
@chapter Crate @code{gpui-miniapp}
@cindex gpui-miniapp

@code{gpui-miniapp} is a minimal application shell for GPUI examples
and showcases. It bundles platform-backend selection so individual
demo binaries do not have to re-implement it.

@menu
* gpui-miniapp User Guide::
* gpui-miniapp Developer Guide::
@end menu

@node gpui-miniapp User Guide
@section User Guide

End users never see this crate. It exists so the @code{gpui-d3rs} and
@code{gpui-ui-kit} showcase binaries can ship with a few lines of
glue instead of duplicating window-creation boilerplate.

@node gpui-miniapp Developer Guide
@section Developer Guide

@subheading What it provides

@itemize @bullet
@item A function to start a GPUI app from a single setup closure.
@item Platform-backend selection (Metal on macOS, equivalent
  elsewhere) hidden behind a feature flag.
@item A default theme and design-system wiring so showcases look
  consistent.
@end itemize

@subheading Usage

@example
gpui_miniapp::run("Showcase title", |cx| @{
    cx.activate(true);
    cx.open_window(/* @dots{} */, |window, cx| @{
        cx.new(|cx| MyView::new(cx))
    @}).unwrap();
@});
@end example

@subheading When to reach for it

Use it for examples and integration tests. Production apps
(@code{app-gpui}, plugin editors) should configure their own shell so
they can manage menubar items, deep links and IPC explicitly.
